```
$ jci-audit release-prep -h
Release gate: reproducible, pinned-advisory-db validation

Usage: jci-audit release-prep [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -v, --verbose...  Increase logging verbosity
  -q, --quiet...    Decrease logging verbosity
  -h, --help        Print help (see more with '--help')

Version:
      --release-version <VERSION>  The release version being validated (e.g. "1.2.0")
      --version-env <VERSION_ENV>  Env var NAME holding the release version (default SEMVER)

Security:
      --advisory-db <ADVISORY_DB>  Advisory-db root; cargo-deny's checkout lives beneath it

Output:
      --deny-warnings  Fail if the tools report any warning

$ jci-audit release-prep --help
Release gate: reproducible, pinned-advisory-db validation.

Locks `cargo-deny` to the pinned commit and runs it offline; `cargo-audit` runs live as a non-blocking currency check. Writes the record locally to `.security/release-<VERSION>.json`; see jerus-org/jci-audit#75 for how it is distributed from there.

Usage: jci-audit release-prep [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Version:
      --release-version <VERSION>
          The release version being validated (e.g. "1.2.0").
          
          Falls back to an environment variable when omitted, since release pipelines compute the version at runtime.

      --version-env <VERSION_ENV>
          Env var NAME holding the release version (default SEMVER).
          
          Used when --release-version is not given.

Security:
      --advisory-db <ADVISORY_DB>
          Advisory-db root; cargo-deny's checkout lives beneath it.
          
          Its commit becomes the pin. Defaults to ~/.cargo/advisory-db.

Output:
      --deny-warnings
          Fail if the tools report any warning

```
